Something must happen down there.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:04.010
Ah, Mondays and Fridays are our big days.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:07.350
On Mondays, everybody's telling what they did over the weekend,

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.530
and on Fridays, everybody's telling what they plan to do on the weekend.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.490
What do you tell them when they ask you about your weekend?

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.810
I used to tell them the truth, so now they don't ask me anymore.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:26.040
Oh, dear, Wally is a very sweet boy.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.300
What's he being a sweet boy about now?

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.320
He's upstairs helping Beaver with his arithmetic homework.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:34.730
Well, that is nice of Wally.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.040
Arithmetic's always been Beaver's weakest subject.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.800
