00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.230
a D minus. You gave him

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:06.340
a D minus? I know

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:08.420
he's been trying hard, but he failed

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:14.100
two tests. Oh, well

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:16.240
look, Miss Landers, I know you're very busy

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.200
and perhaps we could talk a little bit more about

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:21.300
this on Thursday. Bye.

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:33.410
Hi. Hey, I got it. It's a great little playing kit.

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:34.810
Where's Beaver? I want to give it to him right away.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:37.960
Honey, he's upstairs, but there's something I think we ought to talk about first.

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:42.150
Huh? What's up?

00:16:42.740 --> 00:16:45.000
Well, Miss Landers called me today about a meeting,

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:47.590
and I mentioned Beaver's B-plus in arithmetic.

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:48.090
Yeah?

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:50.050
She said he didn't get a B-plus.

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:52.070
She gave him a D-minus.

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:55.420
Well, did you tell her he had a B-plus on his report card?

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.720
Well, no, I wanted to talk to you first.

00:16:58.200 --> 00:16:59.970
Do you suppose she could have made a mistake?

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.600
and put the mark down wrong?

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:03.890
Well, I guess she could have, but I doubt it.

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:06.240
Where is that report card, anyway?

00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:08.290
It's still in your desk drawer.

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:16.220
Yeah. Why, that little schemer.

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:17.970
What do you mean?

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:18.920
Look at that.

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:21.320
The oldest trick in schoolboy history.

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:24.050
Beaver took a pen, and with just two marks,

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:26.640
he made a D minus into a B plus.

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:28.120
You see there?

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:29.840
The color of the ink's just a shade.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:34.880
Oh, Ward, I can hardly believe Beaver'd do something like this.

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:38.490
Well, he was probably desperate. We put so much pressure on him about arithmetic.

00:17:39.810 --> 00:17:42.590
Well, didn't he know he'd get caught when he took the card back?

00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:47.830
Well, I guess when you're a kid and see a chance to stall off trouble for even an hour,

00:17:48.030 --> 00:17:50.770
you tend to ignore the fact that you're probably gonna be caught.

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:54.030
Well, Ward, I guess you better talk to him.

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:59.630
Yeah, I guess I better. Beaver?

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:02.060
Beaver, would you come down here right away?

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:03.440
Okay, Dad.

00:18:04.300 --> 00:18:05.700
Think you brought home my model plane?

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:07.520
I don't know.

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:10.720
It's a funny way to call you if he's bringing home a present.

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:14.660
What are you doing?

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:18.020
Checking to see if any of these other grades are changed.

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:19.960
You're acting like a detective.

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:22.860
Sometimes you have to to stay ahead of your kids.

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:28.240
Hey, Dad.

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:32.450
I see you got home.

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:34.120
Yes, I got home.

00:18:35.140 --> 00:18:36.340
Is that the model plane?

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:38.600
Yes, that's the model airplane.

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:40.290
Why did you do it, Beaver?

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:43.700
Come downstairs on a kind of dead Comey.

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:49.720
Beaver, on your report card here, it shows a B-plus in arithmetic.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:51.500
Yes, sir.

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:54.100
Is that the mark you think you deserved?

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:58.840
Well, I didn't really think so, but I didn't want to make a big fuss.

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:00.850
Oh, you didn't?

00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:04.070
A guy should not tell his teacher she goofed something up.

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:07.950
She might think I was calling her dumb and get mad and flunk me in all my subjects.

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:12.050
Beaver, I don't think that's a very good explanation at all.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:15.840
Neither do I, but I'm not very good at explanations.

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:18.340
Beaver, I spoke to Miss Landers today.

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:21.590
She didn't give you a B+, she gave you a D-.

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:24.440
How come it came out of B+.

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:27.630
We know how it came out of B+.

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:29.770
The mark was changed.

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:33.280
Yeah, it was changed all right.

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:34.740
I wonder who did that.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:36.540
Well, we know that, too.

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:39.570
Look, son, I can see how it happened.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:43.540
You saw that D-minus, and you knew that when I saw it, I'd be upset.

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:47.300
So to keep out of trouble, you took a pen and changed the mark.

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:48.470
Now, isn't that what happened?

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:51.730
What happens if I say no?

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:55.130
You're in a lot worse trouble than you're in now.

00:19:57.120 --> 00:19:58.180
Then I don't know what to say.

00:19:58.970 --> 00:19:59.980
Beaver, why...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.820
Why didn't you just come right out and say you changed the mark?

00:20:03.420 --> 00:20:04.640
Because I don't want to be a liar.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.820
Beaver, are you really going to stick to that story?

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:10.420
Gee, Dad, it's the only story you got. You got to stick to it.

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:14.730
All right, son, I don't want to hear any more about it now or discuss it any further.

00:20:15.620 --> 00:20:18.460
You go on up to your room and wait there while your mother and I talk about this.

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:19.980
Yes, sir.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:27.190
Don't worry, Dad. I won't run away or anything.

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:29.910
I'll give you and Mom plenty of time to decide.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:30.920
how to be mean to me.

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:39.280
Poor Beaver's always admitted before when he was wrong.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:41.680
Now, why is he sticking to this story?

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:43.280
I don't know.

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:46.000
Probably because he's growing up.

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:50.850
Beave, where's your present?

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:54.640
Gee, Wally, what'd you want to go and be a wise guy for?

00:20:58.080 --> 00:20:58.800
What's the matter?

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:05.370
Dad thinks I changed my grade in arithmetic from a D minus to a B plus.

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:11.500
Beaver, you wouldn't do anything like that.

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:14.310
How come you didn't just tell him that you didn't do it?

00:21:14.740 --> 00:21:15.860
Well, I kept telling him.

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:20.090
What's the good of telling him anything if they got it in their mind that you're a no-good kid?

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:23.860
But, heck, Dad's usually pretty fair.

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:26.700
How come he's so sure that the mark was changed?

00:21:27.690 --> 00:21:29.510
He showed me the report card and everything.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:31.480
It's even got a different color ink.

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:36.010
Hey, Wally.

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:37.840
Yeah?

00:21:38.550 --> 00:21:40.430
You think maybe an angel could have changed it?

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:42.100
Nah.

00:21:42.520 --> 00:21:44.760
Angels just save guys from drowning and stuff.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:46.980
They never mess with report cards.

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:52.230
Hey, you know, I was just thinking here.

00:21:53.070 --> 00:21:54.470
Eddie and Lumpy were hanging around

00:21:54.470 --> 00:21:56.410
when Gilbert brought the report card over.

00:21:59.040 --> 00:21:59.680
Wait a minute.

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:05.620
Wait a minute. I think I'll go over and have a talk with that, Eddie.

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:11.150
Gee, Wally. Why would he change the mark of my report card? He's your best friend.

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:15.240
Yeah, I know he's my best friend. I also know he's a crummy creep.

00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:29.900
Yes, Eddie. I see, Eddie. Well, I think that was about the worst joke.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:30.820
I ever heard of.

00:22:31.390 --> 00:22:33.390
Oh, I agree with you, Mr. Cleaver, sir.

00:22:34.420 --> 00:22:35.920
I probably wouldn't have done it

00:22:35.920 --> 00:22:37.840
if Clarence hadn't have been there to urge me on.

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:40.560
I hope that my calling like this

00:22:40.560 --> 00:22:42.620
will keep you from harboring a grudge against me.

00:22:43.660 --> 00:22:44.200
All right, Eddie.

00:22:44.860 --> 00:22:46.860
But if you ever pull a trick like this again,

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:48.820
I don't want to ever see you around this house.

00:22:48.940 --> 00:22:49.380
Do you understand?

00:22:50.380 --> 00:22:51.180
Oh, yes, sir.

00:22:52.150 --> 00:22:53.890
Thank you for being so understanding.

00:22:55.240 --> 00:22:55.780
Yes, sir.

00:22:56.220 --> 00:22:56.880
Thank you, sir.

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:02.600
Is that good enough for you, Wally?

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:05.500
Yeah, that was just about good enough, Eddie.

00:23:06.550 --> 00:23:09.430
If you ever pull another trick like this again, I'm gonna murder you.

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:10.800
Okay, okay.

00:23:11.330 --> 00:23:12.710
But you're gonna have to stand in line,

00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:14.710
because your pop's gonna murder me first.

00:23:15.940 --> 00:23:17.260
Eddie admitted it, huh?

00:23:17.880 --> 00:23:21.920
Yeah, but I somehow got the impression that Wally was around somewhere,

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:23.080
twisting his arm a little.

00:23:24.810 --> 00:23:26.650
Well, you told Beaver he was wrong.

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:29.320
Now I guess you're going to have to tell him he's right.

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:31.600
Yeah.

00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:38.790
You know, it's so easy to tell them when they're wrong

00:23:38.790 --> 00:23:40.690
and so hard to tell them when they're right.

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:43.830
I'll go with you, dear. We'll tell them together.

00:23:46.400 --> 00:23:47.820
I just hope Beaver will forgive us.

00:23:48.200 --> 00:23:51.010
Well, we've got one good thing working for us here.

00:23:51.470 --> 00:23:53.750
When a kid's Beaver's age, you can be pretty wrong

00:23:53.750 --> 00:23:57.130
or pretty unjust to him and still wind up with a great big hug.

00:23:57.930 --> 00:23:59.690
You think Beaver's outgrown that stage?

00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:02.820
Well, I hope not. I'll be pretty disappointed if he has.

00:24:05.580 --> 00:24:22.430
How come he didn't read the doorbell?

00:24:23.050 --> 00:24:26.490
Well, I didn't know if you were home, and I didn't want to talk to any grown-ups.

00:24:26.770 --> 00:24:29.980
Oh. Hey, Peeve, I haven't seen you for a couple of days. What's...

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:33.440
Well, you know when you gave my report card to Lumpy and Eddie?

00:24:33.660 --> 00:24:36.940
Well, they changed my arithmetic grade from a D minus to a B plus.

00:24:37.300 --> 00:24:41.340
Then my father brought me a present, but he didn't give it to me on account that he thought I did it.

00:24:41.590 --> 00:24:45.800
Well, so he yelled at me. Then he found out Eddie and Lumpy did it, so he said he was sorry,

00:24:45.880 --> 00:24:49.570
and I said okay, but I didn't get the present anyways on account that I got a D minus.

00:24:51.070 --> 00:24:53.350
Oh. What's new with you?

00:24:53.880 --> 00:24:55.180
Nothing new with me, either.

00:25:01.760 --> 00:25:02.180
You

00:26:05.620 --> 00:26:08.000
How come you didn't ring the doorbell?

00:26:08.620 --> 00:26:10.020
Well, I didn't know if you were home,

00:26:10.120 --> 00:26:12.040
and I didn't want to talk to any grown-ups.

00:26:12.760 --> 00:26:15.150
Hey, Eve, I haven't seen you for a couple of days.

00:26:15.310 --> 00:26:15.830
What's new?

00:26:16.920 --> 00:26:19.000
Well, you know when you gave my report card to Lumpy and Eddie?

00:26:19.260 --> 00:26:22.460
Well, they changed my arithmetic grade from a D- to a B+.

00:26:22.840 --> 00:26:24.460
Then my father brought me a present,

00:26:24.810 --> 00:26:26.930
but he didn't give it to me on account of he thought I did it.

00:26:27.110 --> 00:26:28.310
Well, so he yelled at me.

00:26:28.980 --> 00:26:29.980
Then he found that Eddie and Lumpy...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.100
so he said he was sorry, and I said, okay,

00:26:32.640 --> 00:26:33.900
but I didn't get the present anyways,

00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:35.140
and I kinda got a D minus.

00:26:36.660 --> 00:26:38.910
Oh, what's new with you?

00:26:39.460 --> 00:26:40.740
Nothing new with me, either.
